error: Invalid capsule tier: "InvalidTier"

       Computational capsule tiers define optimization strategies.

       Valid tiers (UCE34 Framework):

       Foundation Tiers (1-6):
       - Atomic:      Lockfree coordination (3-10× speedup)
       Example: DualAtomicU64, CircuitBreaker (<5ns)

       - SIMD:        Vectorized computation (2-19× speedup)
       Example: SimdF32x8 (8-lane parallel, 19× Hebbian learning)

       - FixedPoint:  Deterministic precision (2-10× speedup)
       Example: Q16.16 (83.4ns P&L calculations)

       - Batch:       Throughput processing (10-100× speedup)
       Example: ParallelBatchProcessor (9.6× compound)

       - Streaming:   Continuous computation (O(1) incremental)
       Example: AsyncLogCapsule (<50ns append)

       - Mixed:       Hybrid multi-tier (50-100× compound speedup)
       Example: T1+T2+T3 full composite (24× compound)

       Extended Tiers (7-10):
       - GPU:          Accelerator computing (100-1000× speedup)
       - Network:      Zero-copy networking (10-50× speedup)
       - Persistent:   Crash-safe storage (mmap-backed)
       - Probabilistic: Approximate algorithms (100-1000× memory reduction)

       Phase 3 P2: Tier inference available!
       If tier not specified, the macro will infer from field types:
       - AtomicU64 → Atomic
       - Simd types → SIMD
       - Q8_8/Q16_16 → FixedPoint
       - Multiple → Mixed

       Fix:
       #[capsule(alignment = 64, tier = "Atomic")]

       Help: Use tier = "Atomic" for most capsules or omit for auto-inference
       See: /home/samuel/Docs/The Computational Capsule.md (Section: Tier Selection)
       See: UCE34_FRAMEWORK.md Q10-Q12 (Tier Selection Guide)
       See: $WORKSPACE/atomic_capsule/CLAUDE.md (100+ tier examples)
